  "problem": "Expressed as a mixed number in its lowest terms, $6\\times \\frac{7}{8}=${{field-1}}.",
  "worked_solution": "To multiply a fraction by a whole number, we multiply the fraction's numerator by the whole number and keep the denominator the same:\n\n$$\n\\frac{6\\times 7}{8}=\\frac{42}{8}\n$$\n\nWe then simplify:\n\n$$\n\\frac{42}{8}=\\frac{42÷2}{8÷2}=\\frac{21}{4}\n$$\n\nFinally, we then convert $\\frac{21}{4}$ to a mixed number:\n\n$$\n21÷4=5\\,\\text{R}\\,1=5\\,\\frac{1}{4}\n$$",
